{"parentUuid":"10841ecc-5805-4815-adb9-d450458facb4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BRHeQDfMxo9y86SME5aUFg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are concrete examples of **first-time contribution guides** — i.e. dedicated onboarding paths separate from a generic `CONTRIBUTING.md`:\n\n**Tutorial-style repos** (the whole repo *is* the guide; you practice by contributing to it):\n- [firstcontributions/first-contributions](https://github.com/firstcontributions/first-contributions) — walk through fork → edit → PR against the repo itself. ~50k+ contributors have used it as their literal first PR.\n- [freeCodeCamp/how-to-contribute-to-open-source](https://github.com/freeCodeCamp/how-to-contribute-to-open-source) — long-form guide with project lists curated for newcomers.\n- [First Timers Only](https://www.firsttimersonly.com/) and the `first-timers-only` issue label convention.\n\n**Project-specific \"your first PR\" docs** (separate from CONTRIBUTING.md):\n- [Rust — \"Getting Started\" in rustc-dev-guide](https://rustc-dev-guide.rust-lang.org/getting-started.html) — a whole chapter for first-time compiler contributors, distinct from the generic CONTRIBUTING.\n- [Kubernetes contributor guide — \"Your First Contribution\"](https://www.kubernetes.dev/docs/guide/contributing/#your-first-contribution) — explicit phased path before the main contributor docs.\n- [Home Assistant — \"Start developing\"](https://developers.home-assistant.io/docs/development_index) walkthrough.\n- [TensorFlow — \"Contributor guide\" with a beginner track](https://www.tensorflow.org/community/contribute).\n- [Node.js — `doc/contributing/pull-requests.md`](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/main/doc/contributing/pull-requests.md) — step-by-step PR walkthrough aimed at first-timers, paired with the higher-level CONTRIBUTING.md.\n\n**GitHub-native convention:**\n- Any repo's `/contribute` page (e.g. [facebook/react/contribute](